  "review_notes": "The file has one declaration, Prod.Lex.toLexOrderHom. It is a bundled OrderHom wrapper around toLex, built from Prod.Lex.toLex_mono. I grepped Mathlib for other bundled order homs or embeddings of toLex on products, and for related names such as toLexOrderEmb. I found none, so there is no competing concept. The only uses are in Algebra/Order/Monoid/Lex.lean, where it is composed with inl and inr. A named bundled hom is a legitimate API, and the unbundled monotonicity lemma it wraps is not a duplicate. I abstain.",
